  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-135564",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We are given the following situation for each month:\n\n- From the customers that prefer chain $A,$ $5%$ change to chain $B$ and $15%$ change to chain $C.$ This implies that $80%$ of them continue to prefer chain $A.$\n\n- From the customers that prefer chain $B,$ $25%$ change to chain $A$ and $25%$ change to chain $C.$ This implies that $50%$ of them continue to prefer chain $B.$\n\n- From the customers that prefer chain $C,$ $15%$ change to chain $A$ and $35%$ change to chain $B.$ This implies that $50%$ of them continue to prefer chain $C.$\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td colspan=\"3\" align=\"center\">From:</td> \n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Chain A</b></td>\n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Chain B</b></td>\n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Chain C</b></td> \n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td rowspan=\"3\" align=\"center\">To:</td>\n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Chain A</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.15$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Chain B</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.05$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Chain C</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.15$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe can write the corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.8 & 0.25 & 0.15 \\\\ 0.05 & 0.5 & 0.35 \\\\ 0.15 & 0.25 & 0.5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=0.25+0.05+0.5=0.8.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
